    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"National Grid Corporation Limited is the overarching organization responsible for managing grid production technology renovation and equipment overhaul projects. It establishes regulations, standards, and supervisory frameworks for project feasibility studies and approvals across its headquarters, branches, and affiliated units.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project feasibility study refers to either a project feasibility report or a project proposal. It is a critical outcome of the pre-project phase, serving as the foundation for project reserve, planning, design, implementation, and adjustment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Equipment Department is the primary management department responsible for grid production technology renovation and equipment overhaul work. It enforces national laws, industry standards, and company regulations; develops management rules and technical standards; and oversees, supervises, and evaluates feasibility study processes. It also conducts review and approval for key projects (e.g., those above scale limits, headquarters-funded, inter-provincial entrusted operation assets, and other major projects).\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网发展部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Development Department participates in the review of key project feasibility studies, contributing to strategic planning and project evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Finance Department participates in the review of key project feasibility studies and conducts economic and financial compliance reviews.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部安质部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Branch Safety and Quality Department is the designated management unit for grid production technology renovation and equipment overhaul within the branch. It implements company-level regulations, organizes feasibility study preparation and preliminary review for projects under its jurisdiction, approves feasibility studies for projects funded by the branch, and supports central headquarters in project reviews.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部规划统计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Branch Planning and Statistics Department participates in the preliminary review of key projects funded by the branch and the review of lower-tier projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Branch Finance Department participates in the preliminary review of key projects funded by the branch and the review of lower-tier projects, and conducts economic and financial compliance evaluations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Provincial Company Equipment Management Department is the primary management unit at the provincial level. It ensures compliance with company regulations, supervises and evaluates feasibility study work, organizes feasibility study preparation for projects under its operation, approves feasibility studies for projects below scale limits, conducts preliminary reviews for large-scale projects, and coordinates with higher-level entities on project approval processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发展部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Development Department at the provincial level participates in project feasibility study reviews, contributing to strategic alignment and planning.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"财务部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Finance Department at the provincial level participates in project feasibility study reviews and conducts economic and financial compliance evaluations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地市级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Municipal-level Company Equipment Management Department is the primary management body responsible for organizing feasibility study preparation, review, and approval of projects within its jurisdiction (including county power supply enterprises). It conducts preliminary reviews for projects under provincial approval authority and oversees and evaluates feasibility study work.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"