    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"站用电系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The station power system refers to the electrical system responsible for supplying power to auxiliary equipment in a substation. It includes the wiring configuration, distribution device layout, and equipment selection requirements. A significant change in system capacity necessitates a station load calculation and determination of station transformer selection.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"照明系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The lighting system encompasses the current state of lighting in the substation, including modifications to working and emergency lighting, illumination levels in key areas, control methods, and luminaire selection criteria.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"防雷接地系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The lightning protection and grounding system involves protective measures for equipment and buildings during renovation. It includes soil resistivity, existing grounding network status, proposed grounding system design, technical principles for grounding devices, and calculations for touch and step potential.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"二次设备接地\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The grounding requirement for secondary equipment ensures safety and proper operation by establishing reliable electrical connections to prevent interference and hazards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统继电保护\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"System relay protection refers to the configuration and upgrade necessity of protection systems related to the project, including line protection, busbar protection, circuit breaker protection, automatic backup switching, fault recording, and microcomputer protection information management subsystems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"变电站自动化系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The substation automation system includes control management modes (such as manned, few-person supervision, unmanned, or integrated dispatching), monitoring and surveillance scope, network architecture, equipment configuration (station level, interval level, process level, network devices), functional implementation, and interface requirements with other systems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"元件保护及自动装置\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"This category covers the protection configuration for key components such as main transformers, station service transformers, and reactive power compensation devices, including sampling, tripping, failure signaling, and fault recording system setup.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"站用交直流电源系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The integrated AC/DC power system for station use includes its structure, functions, monitoring scope, and communication methods. The total monitoring device oversees all aspects of the system.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"直流系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The DC system refers to the direct current power supply system in the substation, including voltage level, wiring method, selection of DC panels, batteries, charging equipment, parameters, and layout. A major capacity change requires DC load statistics and calculations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"不停电电源系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The uninterruptible power supply system is designed to meet the continuous power needs of critical secondary equipment, with defined wiring configurations and setup plans.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"全站时钟同步系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The entire station clock synchronization system provides timing signals to all layers of equipment (station control layer, interval layer, process layer). It specifies interface quantities, specifications, synchronization accuracy, switch requirements, and implementation details, especially when using network-based timing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"非关口电能计量系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The non-portal energy metering system outlines the configuration and networking plan for energy meters at various voltage levels. When using networked data collection, it defines meter configuration and interface requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设备状态监测系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The equipment condition monitoring system is designed based on the monitoring range and parameters of substation equipment. It includes sensor and measurement device configuration, system functionality, and requirements for transmitting data to remote master stations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"辅助控制系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The auxiliary control system includes backend functions for video surveillance, security, fire alarm, transformer fire protection, heating and ventilation, lighting, water supply and drainage, and their interlocking schemes. It also includes interface requirements with remote master systems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"图像监视及安全警卫子系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The video surveillance and security subsystem includes functional design, monitoring coverage, camera placement, and remote transmission scheme for unmanned substations, along with bandwidth and security zoning requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"火灾报警子系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The fire alarm system includes system architecture, cabling requirements, host and control module layout, and integration with other systems for coordinated response.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"环境监测子系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The environmental monitoring subsystem consists of system structure, monitoring scope, sensor placement, and configuration for temperature, humidity, gas levels, etc.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"光缆配置\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The optical fiber cable configuration includes selection, installation, and supporting facilities for each installation unit.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电流互感器、电压互感器二次参数\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"This category covers the selection of secondary parameters for current and voltage transformers, including phase count, number of secondary windings, accuracy class, capacity, and configuration based on different voltage levels and primary connection types.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"二次设备的接地、防雷、抗干扰\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Measures for grounding, lightning protection, and electromagnetic interference mitigation are applied to secondary equipment based on layout and operational requirements. This includes grounding methods for CT secondary circuits and design of equipotential grounding grids.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"二次设备组柜及布置\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The arrangement and cabinet configuration of secondary equipment are specified according to system upgrades, covering station-level, interval-level, process-level, network, and other secondary devices. Basic requirements for cabinet structures are also included.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"站址区域概况\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The site location, geographical conditions, transportation access, and demolition of buildings or structures are described in relation to the substation's construction site.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工程地质和水文气象条件\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"This includes geological strata distribution, tectonic features, and adverse geological phenomena present at the site, along with hydrological and meteorological conditions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"站区总平面布置与交通运输\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The overall layout of the substation area includes outgoing line corridors, adjacent infrastructure, buildings, underground pipelines, roads, green spaces, main entrances, and their connection to external roads, as well as equipment transport logistics.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主要建构筑物情况\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Details about the renovation of key buildings and structures, including materials, foundation designs, types, burial depths, and ground treatment solutions, with possible comparison of multiple technical and economic alternatives.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"采暖通风方案及设备选型\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The heating and ventilation plan includes system design, equipment selection, and professional requirements for duct layout within the substation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"环境保护标准\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Environmental protection standards are determined based on the local environmental quality, special requirements for the substation, changes in pollution sources and pollutants, and initial environmental impact control measures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"环评结论\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The environmental impact assessment conclusion summarizes the findings of the ecological and pollution control evaluation for