    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力电缆\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electric power cables are a key component in the engineering project, with considerations for their installation, safety, and potential hazards to adjacent communication cables.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"通信电缆\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Communication cables are discussed in relation to their proximity to power cables, highlighting potential dangers and required protective measures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"通信光缆\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Communication optical cables are part of the engineering project, with detailed specifications including type, core count, route, length, and installation methods in tunnels, ducts, cable trays, and work wells.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电缆通道\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The cable channel refers to the infrastructure for laying cables, including tunnels, ducts, trenches, and shafts, with design considerations such as dimensions, materials, waterproofing, fire protection, ventilation, and lighting.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工作井\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Work wells are structures used in cable channel construction for access, maintenance, and cable routing, designed based on voltage level, turning radius, and geological conditions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电缆终端站\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The cable terminal station is a facility for connecting cables to the grid, designed according to voltage level, cable routing, and structural requirements including seismic resistance and foundation treatment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电缆登杆（塔）\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Cable ladders (or poles/towers) are structures for mounting cables at transition points, with specified materials and structural details.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"高落差段\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"High drop sections are special environmental segments along the cable path where significant elevation changes may affect cable performance and require special technical handling.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"大坡度段\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Large slope sections refer to areas with steep inclines that may impact cable installation and require specific support and traction measures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"过桥段\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Bridge sections are locations where cables must be routed across bridges, requiring special design and installation considerations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"水下段\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Underwater sections involve cable installation beneath water bodies, necessitating special protective and installation techniques.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"邻近热力管道\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Areas near heating pipelines are considered hazardous due to heat exposure affecting cable insulation and performance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"高土壤热阻段\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Sections with high soil thermal resistance can impair cable heat dissipation, requiring enhanced thermal management during installation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"特殊环境段\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Special environment segments include high drop, large slope, bridge crossings, underwater installations, and proximity to heat sources, each posing unique challenges to cable installation and performance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"敷设方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Installation methods refer to how cables are laid, including selection based on engineering needs, site conditions, load development, and maintenance requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"支撑与固定方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Support and fixation methods are determined by channel type, gradient, and cable installation method, ensuring stability and safety.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"横断面设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Cross-sectional design involves determining dimensions like width, height, structure form, and material thickness of tunnels or ducts, considering cable voltage, bending radius, and environmental factors.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"纵断面设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Longitudinal profile design determines the slope and cover depth of the cable channel, based on municipal planning and geological surveys.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"防水设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Waterproofing design includes sealing the channel body, joints between channels, and interfaces with work wells to prevent water ingress.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"防火设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Fire protection design includes use of fire-resistant troughs, firewalls, and, when necessary, fire monitoring systems and fixed fire suppression devices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"通风设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Ventilation design is required for personnel-accessible cable channels to ensure air quality and safety.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"照明设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Lighting design is implemented in accessible cable channels to provide visibility and operational safety.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"交叉跨越\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Crossing and overpass solutions address interactions with other municipal pipelines and obstacles such as roads, railways, subways, and rivers.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"拆除现状通道\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Removal of existing channels is a task involving demolition work, with associated quantities and logistical planning.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"拆除现状电缆\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Removal of existing cables is part of the project’s scope, requiring estimation of volume and disposal plans.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"施工图卷册安排\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Construction drawing volume arrangement lists the specific volumes and documents produced during the construction phase, including system-side power and communication designs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主要设备材料清册\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The main equipment and material list includes cables, accessories, grounding wires, optical fibers, supports, hardware, steel, civil materials, and related tools, with specifications and quantities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主要拆除设备清单\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The list of major dismantled equipment includes items to be removed, along with disposal recommendations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"概算部分\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The budget section includes cost estimates based on established standards, pricing levels, and various cost components such as static and dynamic investment, land acquisition, and transition measures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网技术改造工程预算定额\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"This is a standard reference document used for budgeting in power grid renovation projects, providing guidelines for cost estimation and calculation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网拆除工程预算定额\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A standardized document used for estimating costs related to the removal of existing electrical infrastructure.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网技术改造工程预算编制与计算标准\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Official standard for preparing and calculating budgets for power grid renovation projects, issued by Guo Neng Dian Li (2010) No. 255.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"20kV及以下配电网工程预算定额\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A set of budgetary standards applicable to distribution networks up to 20kV, used for cost estimation in low-voltage grid projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"20kV及以下配电网工程建设预算编制与计算标准\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Standard for budget preparation in 20kV and below distribution network projects, issued by Guo Neng Dian Li (2009) No. 123.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网检修工程预算定额\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A standard for estimating costs associated with maintenance and repair activities in power grids.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网检修工程预算编制与计算标准\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Official guideline for preparing and calculating budgets for grid maintenance projects, issued by Guo Neng Dian Li (2010) No. 256.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目业主\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The project owner is responsible for initiating and overseeing the implementation of the project, including funding and timeline management.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"建设工期\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Construction schedule refers to the planned duration of the project from start to completion, a key factor in project execution and coordination.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可行性研究评审或批复\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Feasibility study review or approval is a formal evaluation and endorsement process that validates the project's technical and economic viability before proceeding.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"初设概算\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Preliminary design estimate is an early-stage cost projection based on initial design plans, used for financial planning and decision-making.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可行性研究估算投资\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Feasibility study investment estimate is the initial projected cost of the project based on preliminary data and assumptions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"增减原因分析\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Analysis of reasons for cost increases or decreases between feasibility study estimates and preliminary design estimates, used to justify budget adjustments.\")##\n\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力电缆\"<|>\"通信电缆\"<|>\"Power cables pose potential danger to nearby communication cables, necessitating protective measures to prevent interference or damage.\"<|>\"hazard mitigation, electromagnetic interference\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"通信光缆\"<|>\"隧道、沟道、电缆夹层、工作井\"<|>\"Optical cables are installed within tunnels, ducts, cable trays, and work wells, with defined placement and installation methods.\"<|>\"installation location, infrastructure integration\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆通道\"<|>\"横断面设计\"<|>\"The cross-sectional design defines the dimensions and structural features of the cable channel, such as width, height, and material thickness.\"<|>\"design specification, spatial planning\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆通道\"<|>\"纵断面设计\"<|>\"The longitudinal profile design determines the slope and burial depth of the cable channel based on terrain and planning requirements.\"<|>\"geometric layout, topographic adaptation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆通道\"<|>\"防水设计\"<|>\"Waterproofing is integrated into the channel structure and joint areas to prevent moisture infiltration.\"<|>\"structural integrity, environmental protection\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆通道\"<|>\"防火设计\"<|>\"Fire protection measures such as fire barriers and monitoring systems are incorporated into the channel design.\"<|>\"safety compliance, risk prevention\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆通道\"<|>\"通风设计\"<|>\"Ventilation systems are included in channels intended for personnel access to maintain safe air quality.\"<|>\"occupatio