under its jurisdiction, approves feasibility studies for projects funded by the branch, and supports central headquarters in project reviews.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部规划统计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Branch Planning and Statistics Department participates in the preliminary review of key projects funded by the branch and the review of lower-tier projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Branch Finance Department participates in the preliminary review of key projects funded by the branch and the review of lower-tier projects, and conducts economic and financial compliance evaluations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Provincial Company Equipment Management Department is the primary management unit at the provincial level. It ensures compliance with company regulations, supervises and evaluates feasibility study work, organizes feasibility study preparation for projects under its operation, approves feasibility studies for projects below scale limits, conducts preliminary reviews for large-scale projects, and coordinates with higher-level entities on project approval processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发展部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Development Department at the provincial level participates in project feasibility study reviews, contributing to strategic alignment and planning.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"财务部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Finance Department at the provincial level participates in project feasibility study reviews and conducts economic and financial compliance evaluations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地市级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Municipal-level Company Equipment Management Department is the primary management body responsible for organizing feasibility study preparation, review, and approval of projects within its jurisdiction (including county power supply enterprises). It conducts preliminary reviews for projects under provincial approval authority and oversees and evaluates feasibility study work.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网经研院\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Economic Research Institute is responsible for reviewing feasibility studies for key projects and headquarters-affiliated lower-tier projects. It conducts detailed economic and financial compliance reviews, provides timely review opinions, offers business guidance to provincial-level institutes, and manages the expert database for project reviews.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省级经研院\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Provincial Economic Research Institute acts on behalf of divisions, provincial companies, or direct subsidiaries to conduct preliminary reviews of key projects, perform feasibility study reviews within applicable levels, carry out economic and financial compliance assessments, issue review opinions, and provide guidance to municipal-level research institutions. It also manages the provincial-level expert database.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目单位\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Project unit refers to the asset operation and maintenance entity or department responsible for organizing the compilation of project feasibility studies based on project needs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限上项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limited-upward projects include projects exceeding specified scale thresholds, headquarters-funded projects, inter-provincial entrusted operation asset projects, and other major projects designated by headquarters. These require centralized review and approval by higher-level authorities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限下项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limited-downward projects are those below the specified scale threshold. Their feasibility studies are approved by provincial or municipal-level authorities according to delegated responsibilities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目可行性研究报告\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project feasibility report is a comprehensive document required for projects meeting specific investment thresholds. It includes sections such as project overview, necessity, technical solutions, economic and financial compliance, disposal of decommissioned equipment, implementation plan, and special notes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目建议书\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project proposal is an alternative document used for smaller projects that do not meet the threshold for a full feasibility report. It contains essential elements like basic information, necessity, solution, economic and financial compliance, and supporting materials.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"估算书\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Estimate book is a cost document prepared strictly according to industry and company regulations, ensuring legal compliance, reasonable pricing, and accurate budgeting for project costs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"评审会议记录\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Review meeting minutes are formal documents summarizing feedback from reviewers during the feasibility study assessment process. Project units must submit revised drafts within five working days after receiving these records.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目实施条件及临时过渡方案\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project implementation conditions and temporary transition plans are part of the foundational data required for feasibility studies, ensuring operational continuity during construction.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"拟拆除设备主要参数\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"List of main parameters of equipment scheduled for removal is a required component in feasibility studies, aiding in asset valuation and disposal planning.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"反措要求\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Countermeasure requirements refer to technical guidelines and safety measures derived from past incidents or system weaknesses, which must be addressed in project designs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"专项治理文件\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Special governance documents contain targeted directives aimed at resolving specific issues in grid operations, forming part of the regulatory basis for project justification.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"The State Grid Equipment Department operates under the authority and direction of National Grid Corporation Limited, implementing its policies and management standards.\"<|>\"organizational hierarchy, policy enforcement\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网发展部\"<|>\"The State Grid Development Department functions under the broader governance structure of National Grid Corporation Limited, contributing to strategic project evaluation.\"<|>\"strategic coordination, organizational function\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网财务部\"<|>\"The State Grid Finance Department is accountable to National Grid Corporation Limited and supports financial oversight in project feasibility studies.\"<|>\"financial oversight, institutional accountability\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"分部安质部\"<|>\"Branch Safety and Quality Departments are subordinate units that implement National Grid's regulations and coordinate with headquarters on project reviews.\"<|>\"regional implementation, hierarchical responsibility\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"省级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"Provincial Equipment Management Departments execute company-wide policies and manage feasibility studies within their jurisdictions.\"<|>\"decentralized execution, policy implementation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"地市级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"Municipal-level Equipment Management Departments operate under provincial supervision and are responsible for local feasibility study work.\"<|>\"local execution, hierarchical workflow\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网经研院\"<|>\"State Grid Economic Research Institute is directly involved in project review and advisory roles under the umbrella of National Grid Corporation Limited.\"<|>\"technical support, expert review\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"省级经研院\"<|>\"Provincial Economic Research Institutes act on behalf of National Grid’s framework, providing localized review services and expert guidance.\"<|>\"supportive service, regional execution\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"限上项目\"<|>\"The State Grid Equipment Department leads the review and approval of all 'limited-upward' projects, which are defined by scale, funding source, or strategic importance.\"<|>\"project classification, approval authority\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"The State Grid Equipment Department oversees the entire lifecycle of project feasibility studies, including development, review, and approval.\"<|>\"project lifecycle management, regulatory oversight\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"省级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"限下项目\"<|>\"Provincial Equipment Management Departments have approval authority over 'limited-downward' projects, reflecting a tiered decision-making model.\"<|>\"decentralized approval, project classification\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"地市级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"项目单位\"<|>\"Municipal-level equipment departments often serve as project units responsible for initiating and compiling feasibility studies.\"<|>\"functional overlap, operational role\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目单位\"<|>\"项目可行性研究报告\"<|>\"Project units are responsible for organizing the creation of project feasibility reports based on project needs and available data.\"<|>\"document preparation, project initiation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目单位\"<|>\"项目建议书\"<|>\"For smaller projects, project units may prepare project proposals instead of full feasibility reports.\"<|>\"alternative documentation, project scaling\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国网经研院\"<|>\"省级经研院\"<|>\"The State Grid Economic Research Institute provides business guidance and oversight to provincial-level institutes, maintaining consistency in review standards.\"<|>\"supervisory relationship, quality control\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"省级经研院\"<|>\"地市级公司经研所\"<|>\"Provincial Economic Research Institutes offer guidance and support to municipal-level research institutions, promoting standardization in feasibility review practices.\"<|>\"guidance, capacity building\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"估算书\"<|>\"The estimate book is a core component of the project feasibility study, ensuring cost accuracy and compliance.\"<|>\"cost estimation, document integration\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"拟拆除设备主要参数\"<|>\"Information on decommissioned equipment parameters is essential for assessing asset retirement and disposal strategies within the feasibility study.\"<|>\"asset management, decommissioning planning\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"反措要求\"<|>\"Countermeasure requirements are mandatory considerations in project feasibility studies to ensure safety and reliability.\"<|>\"compliance, safety standards\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"专项治理文件\"<|>\"Special governance documents provide the rationale for project necessity and guide technical solutions in feasibility studies.\"<|>\"project justification, regulatory basis\"<|>9)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"project feasibility study, grid infrastructure renewal, organizational hierarchy, financial compliance, project review process, asset management, regulatory framework\")<|COMPLETE|>"
