rs to the second-generation Production Management System used for project management, where migrated projects may have automatic scoring but require manual evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"PMS3.0\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"PMS3.0 is the third-generation Production Management System that requires complete scores including automatic, manual, and composite evaluations for reserve projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"经研院（所）\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Economic Research Institute (or its equivalent) provides formal project review opinions, which must be uploaded and include attachments; these reviews must be valid and linked to the project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"迎峰度夏项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A type of pre-arranged project aimed at addressing grid capacity constraints during peak load periods, particularly related to high-demand seasons, with completion expected by June 30th of the same year.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"预安排项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Projects initiated early due to known future needs such as planned outages, long procurement cycles, or urgent policy implementation, generally not allowed to span fiscal years unless adjusted mid-term.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"年度综合计划项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Annual integrated planning projects that focus on key investment priorities and align with professional work requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"土建工程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Includes construction activities such as tunnel collapse repair, structural crack reinforcement, or tilt correction, which trigger the requirement for an independent feasibility study if costs exceed thresholds.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"独立可研报告\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A standalone feasibility report required for production technology renovation projects exceeding 200 million RMB (inclusive, pre-adjustment, tax-inclusive) or major overhaul projects involving civil engineering over 100 million RMB (exclusive, pre-adjustment).\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目建议书\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A document that can be used instead of a full feasibility study for smaller-scale projects, prepared by the project unit.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"公司总部各专业管理处室\"<|>\"变电专业\"<|>\"The company's professional management departments define the scope and boundaries of the substation specialty, including what equipment belongs to it.\"|>\"professional classification authority\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"公司总部各专业管理处室\"<|>\"通信专业\"<|>\"The headquarters’ management departments determine the professional categorization of communication-related equipment and systems.\"|>\"professional classification authority\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"公司总部各专业管理处室\"<|>\"自动化专业\"<|>\"The headquarters’ management bodies establish the professional boundaries for automation systems and devices.\"|>\"professional classification authority\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"公司总部各专业管理处室\"<|>\"安措专业\"<|>\"The headquarters’ professional management offices assign responsibilities and define inclusion criteria for safety measures projects.\"|>\"professional classification authority\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"小电流接地选线装置\"<|>\"变电专业\"<|>\"In some organizations, small current grounding selection devices located within substations are classified under the substation specialty.\"|>\"equipment classification\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"小电流接地选线装置\"<|>\"保护专业\"<|>\"In certain units, small current grounding selection devices are categorized under the protection specialty rather than substation.\"|>\"equipment classification\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"小电流接地选线装置\"<|>\"配电专业\"<|>\"In ring network cabinets, small current grounding selection devices are classified under the distribution specialty.\"|>\"equipment classification\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"PMS2.0\"<|>\"PMS3.0\"<|>\"PMS2.0 is a legacy system from which projects are migrated into PMS3.0, which has stricter data completeness and scoring requirements.\"|>\"system evolution, data migration\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"经研院（所）\"<|>\"独立可研报告\"<|>\"The Economic Research Institute issues formal review opinions on independent feasibility reports, which must be attached and valid.\"|>\"review authority, documentation requirement\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"迎峰度夏项目\"<|>\"预安排项目\"<|>\"Both are types of pre-planned projects, with 'overload relief' and 'seasonal demand' being key drivers for both, though 'overload relief' is more specific to summer peak loads.\"|>\"project type alignment\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"年度综合计划项目\"<|>\"预安排项目\"<|>\"Both involve forward-looking planning; however, annual comprehensive plans are tied to strategic priorities, while pre-arranged projects are driven by operational urgency and timing.\"|>\"planning cycle alignment\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"土建工程\"<|>\"独立可研报告\"<|>\"Projects involving civil engineering over 100 million RMB require a standalone feasibility report, indicating a direct regulatory link.\"|>\"regulatory compliance, threshold-based requirement\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目建议书\"<|>\"独立可研报告\"<|>\"Project proposals may serve as alternatives to full feasibility studies for smaller projects, but larger projects must submit a full independent feasibility report.\"|>\"document hierarchy, project scale dependency\"<|>8)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"professional classification, project management, feasibility study requirements, equipment categorization, system migration, planning phases, technical documentation, regulatory thresholds\")<|COMPLETE|>"
