    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"249号文\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A regulatory document governing subcontracting management in technical renovation and maintenance projects, referenced as the current standard for compliance, replacing the outdated 74号文.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"74号文\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"An obsolete regulatory document that has been superseded and should no longer be used as a reference for subcontracting practices in project management.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主体工程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Core construction or installation work within a project that must not be outsourced to third parties, including electrical installation and testing of substation and distribution equipment, tower erection, cable laying, and specialized inspection services.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"关键性工程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Critical components or tasks within a project that are essential to its success and cannot be professionally subcontracted, such as primary electrical system installations and major structural repairs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"施工费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The total cost associated with construction activities, defined as the sum of building and installation engineering costs, removal fees, minus materials supplied by the client, plus relevant fees from other expenses.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设计费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A fee charged for design services related to a project, which must be adjusted according to the discount ratio applied in the contract, and is subject to specific calculation rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"监理费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A fee for supervision services, which may be reduced by a coefficient (e.g., ×0.87) depending on the unit's policy, or exempted if no supervision is required.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"基本预备费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A reserve fund typically not included in project estimates unless explicitly justified, and is generally excluded under normal circumstances.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"招标费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A fee associated with the bidding process, which is generally not included in project estimates but may be counted if necessary and supported by documentation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"后评价费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A fee for post-project evaluation, which is typically not included in estimates but may be allowed if properly justified and documented.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"高海拔、严寒、酷热特殊地区\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Geographic conditions specified in regulations where special construction surcharges may be applied, but only if explicitly covered by pre-regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"架空线路工程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A type of infrastructure project involving overhead power lines, which is exempt from nighttime construction surcharge fees according to regulation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"通信线路工程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A category of projects involving communication cables, which does not qualify for nighttime or multiple entry surcharges.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"20kV及以下配网工程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Distribution network projects at or below 20kV voltage level, which are not eligible for multiple entry increase fees.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设备监造费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A fee for supervising equipment manufacturing, which is generally not charged unless the project includes specific high-voltage equipment such as transformers, circuit breakers, and GIS systems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新技术应用研究试验费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A cost associated with research and testing of new technologies, which is not typically included in project estimates unless special circumstances justify it.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新技术项目性能测试费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A fee for evaluating the performance of new technology projects, which is generally excluded unless explicitly permitted and explained.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"甲供物资\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Materials provided by the client (owner), which, if incorrectly handled, could lead to a shift from client-supplied to contractor-supplied status during settlement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"乙供物资\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Materials supplied by the contractor, which may result from improper handling of client-provided materials in procurement processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"等保测评\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"An information security assessment process required for certain projects, whose costs must be accounted for under 'other expenses' per pre-regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全防护费用\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Costs incurred to ensure safety during project execution, which must be included in 'other expenses' as per established regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"固定总价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A pricing model in contracts where the total cost is fixed regardless of actual work performed, used in project acceptance and settlement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"固定单价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A pricing method where each unit of work is priced separately, applicable in both construction and subcontracting agreements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"固定费率\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A payment structure based on a percentage of the base cost, commonly used in contracts requiring discount application for design, supervision, and construction fees.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"审定的施工费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The officially approved construction cost after audit, used as the basis for calculating final payments under fixed-rate contracts.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"农民工工资支付流程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A procedural requirement in labor subcontracting contracts mandating timely and full payment of wages to migrant workers, including transparent reporting and compliance mechanisms.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"劳务分包\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A form of subcontracting focused solely on labor services, which must be clearly priced per person-hour or similar, and cannot be structured as a lump-sum package.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"专业分包\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Subcontracting of technical work that requires specialized skills, which must not include non-labor portions being further subcontracted.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"人员资质水平\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A criterion evaluated in the capacity commitment letter, indicating the qualifications and competence of personnel assigned to a project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可承接工程量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A measure of project capacity defined in the capacity commitment letter, specifying how much work a contractor can realistically handle.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"机械装备及工器具配置\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The equipment and tools available to a contractor, required to be listed in the capacity commitment letter to demonstrate operational readiness.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工期安排\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A schedule outlining the timeline for project completion, included in the capacity commitment letter to ensure feasibility.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"违约责任\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Legal or contractual penalties for failing to meet commitments outlined in the capacity or subcontracting documents.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工作票类型\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Classification of work permits (e.g., first-type or second-type), which must correspond to the scope of work defined in the subcontract agreement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"合同变更\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A formal adjustment to the original contract terms due to changes in scope, quantity, or cost, requiring documentation and approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工程量变更签证\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A written confirmation issued when the actual project volume differs from the contracted amount, used to justify adjustments in settlement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"初设\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Preliminary design phase required for certain projects, mandated when investment exceeds thresholds or involves significant design changes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"概算\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A detailed cost estimate prepared during the preliminary design stage, which must align with the contract’s engineering quantities and values.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"中标通知书\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"An official document confirming the successful bidder, used as a reference point for contract pricing and timing constraints.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"计划下达\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The official release of project implementation plans, which must be in