    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"生产技改项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Production technology renovation projects refer to the use of mature, advanced, and applicable technologies, equipment, processes, and materials to update, improve, and complement existing grid production assets, enhancing their safety, reliability, economy, and meeting intelligent, energy-saving, and environmental protection requirements. These projects result in capital expenditures and form fixed assets.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产设备大修项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Equipment maintenance projects are repair activities conducted under project management to restore assets (including equipment, facilities, and auxiliary facilities) to their original condition and capability. These do not increase the original value of fixed assets and are classified as expense-based expenditures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"固定资产原值\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The original value of fixed assets is a key criterion for determining whether a project falls under production technology renovation or equipment maintenance. For example, if the replacement cost of equipment components reaches 50% or more of the original asset value, it should be classified as a tech renovation project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"特高压套管\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Special high-voltage bushings are components with high cost; their replacement can be classified either as a technology renovation or a maintenance project depending on context.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"输电线路加装、更换110kV及以下避雷器\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Installation or replacement of surge arresters on transmission lines at 110kV and below is categorized as a maintenance project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"杆塔更换\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Replacement of towers on transmission lines exceeding five units is classified as a technology renovation project, while fewer than five units may be treated as maintenance or renovation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电缆更换\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Cable replacement is determined based on proportion: if less than 50% of the line's asset value is replaced, it is considered maintenance; otherwise, it is classified as technology renovation. High-voltage power cables (10kV and above) are generally included in technology renovation projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"备品备件补充\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Supplementing spare parts is classified as a cost-type project and should not be included in production technology renovation projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"监控设备整套维修\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Complete maintenance of monitoring systems without involving the main host can be included in maintenance projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网基建项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Grid infrastructure projects involve expanding grid scale or capacity, such as entire substations or lines, and improvements like full transformer or interval upgrades that enhance transmission capability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"配电自动化新建或整体改造\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"New or comprehensive renovations of distribution automation systems, especially when independent of the primary system and investment exceeds several million yuan, are managed under grid infrastructure procedures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主变新增\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Addition of main transformers is included in infrastructure projects. In principle, capacity expansion of main transformers should also be part of infrastructure, but under exceptional circumstances may be included in technology renovation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"配电变压器改造、增容、更换、新增布点\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Distribution transformer upgrades, capacity increases, replacements, and new installations are generally included in distribution network engineering; only when distribution network engineering cannot meet needs are they considered for production technology renovation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"同一单位的主变轮调\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Rotation of main transformers within the same unit is classified as a maintenance project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新增开关柜\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Adding switchgear without increasing outgoing lines can be classified as a technology renovation project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"增加出线间隔/馈线间隔\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Adding outgoing or feeder intervals must be classified as a grid infrastructure project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产辅助基建项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Production auxiliary infrastructure projects include new construction, expansion, or acquisition of buildings and supporting facilities used for operational services such as dispatch control, production management, operation and maintenance, marketing services, material storage, scientific research, training, etc.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产辅助技改与大修项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Production auxiliary renovation and maintenance projects cover renovations and repairs of non-production buildings (e.g., office buildings, conference centers, training centers, hospitals, standalone garages) and their associated equipment and facilities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"视频会议显示屏及相关设备\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Addition, modification, or repair of video conferencing displays and related equipment—excluding those in operational business areas such as dispatch control centers—is classified as a production auxiliary renovation project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"仓储设施、特种车辆车库、无人机库房等\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Renovations or repairs of storage facilities, specialized vehicle garages, drone hangars, live-line operation warehouses, and communication/automation server rooms are classified as tech renovation or maintenance projects. New construction or expansion is classified as production auxiliary infrastructure.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"变电站内生产房屋新建\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"New construction of production buildings within substations (such as control rooms, distribution rooms, protection rooms) or transmission inspection stations can be included in production technology renovation projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"低压接户线以上设备\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Equipment located above low-voltage service lines (i.e., upstream of customer meters) falls under the scope of production technology renovation and maintenance projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"贸易结算计量装置更换\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Replacement of trade settlement metering devices is classified as a marketing project, not a production technology renovation project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"固定资产零购项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Fixed asset zero-purchase projects refer to items listed in the company’s fixed asset directory that can function independently, require no construction or installation work, and are typically instruments, tools, or transportation vehicles.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"有安装工程量的仪器仪表、工器具\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"New additions or modifications to instruments and tools requiring installation work (e.g., voltage monitors, patrol robots, drone charging stations) are classified as production technology renovation projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"数字化项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Digitalization projects involve investments in enterprise information integration platforms, business applications, and information security systems. They focus on management information equipment and include pure software systems and platform constructions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产用监控、操作系统改造\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Modifications and maintenance of production monitoring systems and operating systems can be included in production technology renovation or maintenance projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"配抢指挥平台\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Construction, renovation, or operation/maintenance of the distribution fault command platform, being a PMS functional module, should not be included in production technology renovation or maintenance projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各管理系统之间的接口集成\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Integration between different management systems is not considered part of production technology renovation or maintenance projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"纯三区、四区的软件改造项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Pure software upgrades in Zones III and IV are excluded from technology renovation and should be classified as digitalization projects, such as the new dispatch system (Zone III), which is treated as an independent secondary project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"独立建筑的专用生产性数据中心\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Upgrades and defect elimination of dedicated production data centers in independent buildings fall under digitalization projects for software and hardware. However, the supporting infrastructure (e.g., building, power supply, HVAC, fire protection, access control, video systems) that supports these operations and serves grid production are included in production technology renovation or maintenance projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"日常费用项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Daily operational expenses include routine maintenance tasks such as patrols, cleaning (including live-line washing), upkeep, periodic comprehensive inspections, minor repairs, testing, calibration, labeling maintenance, tree trimming along corridors, snow removal, grass cutting, building repairs, vehicle checks, and replacement of low-value consumables (e.g., standard lighting fixtures, sockets, circuit breakers).\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"因规则变化导致的批量更换标识\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Bulk replacement of device labels due to changes in regulations or standards is classified as a maintenance project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目合并与拆分\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"To reduce complexity and workload, projects of the same voltage level and type can be combined into one project. This includes simultaneous one- and two-level equipment upgrades within the same station or line, or across different voltage levels. Projects must clearly list equipment details and implementation plans in feasibility studies.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"《生产技术改造和设备大修项目编报规范》\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"This document outlines the standardized reporting requirements for production technology renovation and equipment maintenance projects, including accurate classification, project name format, and content description.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网+单位名称\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"A naming convention used in project titles to indicate the state grid company unit (e.g., provincial, municipal, or county power supply company).\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"变电站/线路电压等级和名称\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Specifies the voltage level and 