quantity calculations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"典型设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '典型设计' refers to standardized designs used for towers or components, validated through experience or analysis.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新型杆塔\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '新型杆塔' is a non-standard tower type introduced for new applications, requiring technical and economic evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新型基础\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '新型基础' is an innovative foundation type evaluated for technical feasibility, cost-effectiveness, safety, and constructability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"特殊地段\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '特殊地段' refers to areas with challenging terrain, geology, or environmental conditions requiring special design measures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"重冰地段\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '重冰地段' is a geographical area prone to ice accumulation, impacting conductor and insulator design.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"林区\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '林区' is a forested region along the route, influencing clearance and vegetation management requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主要河流\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '主要河流' are significant water bodies crossed by the transmission line, requiring special crossing design.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"城镇规划\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '城镇规划' refers to urban development plans that affect the selection and alignment of the transmission route.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"海拔高度\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '海拔高度' is a topographical factor influencing meteorological conditions and insulation performance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地形\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '地形' describes the physical landscape along the route, affecting construction and transportation logistics.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地质\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '地质' refers to subsurface conditions such as soil type and rock composition, critical for foundation design.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"水文\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '水文' includes surface and groundwater characteristics affecting foundation stability and drainage.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"交通运输条件\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '交通运输条件' describe road access and transport feasibility for materials and equipment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电信线路\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '电信线路' are communication lines affected by electromagnetic interference from the power line.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"无线电台(站)\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The '无线电台(站)' are radio transmission facilities potentially impacted by electromagnetic fields from the power line.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"资料来源\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '资料来源' refers to the origin of data used in meteorological and geological analyses, including documentation and references.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"换算过程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '换算过程' is a methodological step used to convert raw data into design values, particularly for meteorological parameters.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分析比较\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '分析比较' is a process applied to evaluate different design options based on technical and economic criteria.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"技术经济比较与论证结果\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '技术经济比较与论证结果' summarize the evaluation of alternative schemes using technical and financial metrics.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"路径推荐方案\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '路径推荐方案' is the final proposed route selected after comprehensive evaluation of alternatives.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设计气象条件组合表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '设计气象条件组合表' is a compiled document listing all relevant meteorological conditions used in structural and insulation design.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"导、地线电气特性表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '导、地线电气特性表' contains detailed electrical properties of conductors and ground wires for design use.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"光缆物理特性表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '光缆物理特性表' lists mechanical and physical attributes of optical cables for integration with the power line.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"绝缘子主要尺寸及机电特性表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '绝缘子主要尺寸及机电特性表' provides key dimensions and mechanical/electrical performance data for insulators.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地线绝缘子机械电气特性表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '地线绝缘子机械电气特性表' details the mechanical and electrical properties of insulators used on ground wires.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"单基杆塔的耗材量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '单基杆塔的耗材量' refers to the amount of materials used per tower, including steel and other components.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主材类型和型号\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '主材类型和型号' specify the material grades and models used in tower construction.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"标准高度\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '标准高度' is the typical elevation of towers used in the project, influencing clearance and sag calculations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工程特点\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '工程特点' refer to unique aspects of the project such as geography, environment, and technical complexity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"利用的原有杆塔\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '利用的原有杆塔' are existing towers being reused, subject to verification of design compliance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"验算\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '验算' is a technical check performed to confirm that existing or modified components meet current design standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"适用性结论\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '适用性结论' is the result of a technical assessment indicating whether a component is suitable for use.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"使用性要求\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '使用性要求' are conditions under which an existing tower may be safely reused.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"技术经济特点\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '技术经济特点' describe the balance between innovation, cost, and efficiency of new components.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"使用意义\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '使用意义' refers to the practical or strategic benefit of adopting a new design or technology.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全性和施工可行性\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '安全性和施工可行性' are evaluated for new foundation types to ensure they can be implemented safely and effectively.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"开挖方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '开挖方式' refers to the method used to excavate for foundations, especially in special geological zones.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"特殊措施\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '特殊措施' are additional actions taken to address challenges in difficult or sensitive areas.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"控制标准\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '控制标准' are predefined limits for managing crossings over other infrastructure.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"处理原则\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '处理原则' guide how to manage and resolve issues arising from crossings.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"影响范围\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '影响范围' defines the extent of potential disruption caused by a crossing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"相关数量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '相关数量' refers to the estimated number of crossings or affected elements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"初步停电计划\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '初步停电计划' is a draft schedule outlining when and how outages will occur during the renovation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"建议\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '建议' are recommendations made by the design team to improve project execution and address risks.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统通信配置现状\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '系统通信配置现状' describes the current state of communication systems supporting the power network.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"改扩建需求\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '改扩建需求' are the requirements for upgrading or expanding communication and automation systems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"专业配合要求\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '专业配合要求' define how different engineering disciplines must coordinate their work.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"隶属本线路工程范围\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '隶属本线路工程范围' specifies which components fall under the scope of this project.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"工程项目主要技术经济指标表\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '工程项目主要技术经济指标表' is a summary document compiling key performance and cost metrics.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"改造原因\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '改造原因' is the justification for undertaking the renovation, such as aging infrastructure or system upgrades.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"期望达到的目标\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '期望达到的目标' are the intended outcomes of the renovation, such as improved reliability or capacity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"采用的主要规范和标准\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '采用的主要规范和标准' are official codes and guidelines followed in the design process.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"改造方案采用的主要原则\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '改造方案采用的主要原则' are guiding philosophies behind the design, such as safety, cost-efficiency, or sustainability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"存在问题\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '存在问题' are identified challenges or unresolved issues in the project’s execution or planning.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"明确与前期工程的衔接和配合\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '明确与前期工程的衔接和配合' ensures continuity and integration with previous project phases.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统作用和地位\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '系统作用和地位' describe the function and importance of the line within the broader power network.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"配套系统\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '配套系统' are auxiliary systems such as protection, automation, and communication that support the main power line.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"停电影响\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '停电影响' assesses the consequences of planned outages on system operation and users.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"临时搭接或临时送电线路的方案设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '临时搭接或临时送电线路的方案设计' is an optional but important part of the outage plan.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统侧电源仓\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '系统侧电源仓' refers to the power source side of the system, involved in the design of communication and integration.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"系统通信的施工图设计目录\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '系统通信的施工图设计目录' is part of the overall construction drawing arrangement, detailing communication system drawings.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新建电缆通道\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '新建电缆通道' is a newly constructed pathway for cable installation, distinct from existing ones.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"已建电缆通道\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '已建电缆通道' are pre-existing conduits or tunnels used for cable routing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"典型及特殊路段现状实景照片\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '典型及特殊路段现状实景照片' are visual records used to support design decisions for complex areas.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地下管线断面图\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '地下管线断面图' illustrates the cross-sectional layout of underground utilities at key points.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目可行性研究报告\"<|>\"总论部分\"<|>\"The '项目可行性研究报告' is explicitly cited as a primary design basis in the '总论部分'.<|>\"design foundation, project initiation\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"上级部门或业主单位\"<|>\"总论部分\"<|>\"The '上级部门或业主单位' is listed as a source of special requirements that influence the '总论部分'.<|>\"stakeholder input, project governance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"技术协议书\"<|>\"总论部分\"<|>\"The '技术协议书' is referenced alongside meeting minutes as part of the design basis in the '总论部分'.<|>\"contractual basis, technical compliance\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"会议纪要\"<|>\"总论部分\"<|>\"The '会议纪要' are included among the design references in the '总论部分'.<|>\"meeting outcomes, project alignment\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"系统最大短路电流\"<|>\"电力电缆及其附件的选型\"<|>\"The '系统最大短路电流' is used to determine the cross-sectional area of cables and accessories.<|>\"thermal stability, design calculation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆持续允许载流量\"<|>\"电力电缆及其附件的选型\"<|>\"The '电缆持续允许载流量' is derived from environmental and soil data and is essential for cable sizing.<|>\"thermal rating, design criterion\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"雷电过电压水平\"<|>\"过电压保护、接地、分段和通信干扰\"<|>\"The '雷电过电压 level' directly informs the overvoltage protection strategy.<|>\"protection design, safety standard\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"交叉互联线\"<|>\"过电压保护、接地、分段和通信干扰\"<|>\"The '交叉互联线' is selected based on short-circuit and grounding requirements.<|>\"system protection, grounding design\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"接地线\"<|>\"过电压保护、接地、分段和通信干扰\"<|>\"The '接地线' is sized based on short-circuit current and grounding method.<|>\"grounding system, fault protection\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆护层的过电压保护方案\"<|>\"过电压保护、接地、分段和通信干扰\"<|>\"The 'protective scheme' is specifically designed to shield the cable sheath from overvoltage.<|>\"sheath protection, surge control\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆分段长度\"<|>\"过电压保护、接地、分段和通信干扰\"<|>\"The 'cable segment length' affects grounding configuration and fault current distribution.<|>\"segmentation, grounding practice\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆接头的排列布置\"<|>\"电力电缆及其附件的选型\"<|>\"The 'arrangement' of joints depends on the cable routing and channel layout.<|>\"splicing, spatial planning\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"新建、已建电缆通道\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'new and existing channels' are integral to defining the cable route and access points.<|>\"infrastructure integration, routing\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"工作井\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'work wells' are part of the path planning and are located based on route alignment.<|>\"access point, construction staging\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电缆夹层\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'cable tray' is a location where cables are routed and supported along the path.<|>\"support structure, routing\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"竖井\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'shaft' is a vertical element in the path, requiring special design consideration.<|>\"vertical routing, access\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"地下管线\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'underground pipelines' are obstacles that must be avoided or coordinated with during path planning.<|>\"obstacle avoidance, utility coordination\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"规划配合\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'planning coordination' ensures that the route aligns with future urban or regional development.<|>\"urban integration, long-term planning\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"协议落实\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'agreement implementation' confirms that all necessary permissions and agreements are secured before construction.<|>\"compliance, legal readiness\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"临时搭接\"<|>\"停电方案设计\"<|>\"The 'temporary connection' is a component of the 'outage plan' to maintain service during construction.<|>\"temporary solution, outage mitigation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"临时送电线路\"<|>\"停电方案设计\"<|>\"The 'temporary power line' is another method to sustain power during planned outages.<|>\"temporary power, outage management\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"运行维护工器具\"<|>\"主要设备材料清册\"<|>\"The 'maintenance tools' are listed in the 'material list' if included in procurement.<|>\"procurement item, lifecycle support\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"备品备件\"<|>\"主要设备材料清册\"<|>\"The 'spare parts' are included in the 'material list' for future maintenance needs.<|>\"spare inventory, maintenance planning\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"设备材料损耗\"<|>\"主要设备材料清册\"<|>\"The 'material loss' is accounted for in the total quantities listed in the 'material list'.<|>\"quantity adjustment, procurement accuracy\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"典型设计\"<|>\"杆塔型式\"<|>\"The 'typical design' is used as a benchmark for selecting tower types.<|>\"standardization, design efficiency\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"新型杆塔\"<|>\"杆塔型式\"<|>\"The 'new tower type' requires technical and economic evaluation before adoption.<|>\"innovation, design validation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"新型基础\"<|>\"基础型式\"<|>\"The 'new foundation type' is assessed for feasibility, safety, and cost.<|>\"construction innovation, risk assessment\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"特殊地段\"<|>\"地质概况\"<|>\"The 'special areas' are highlighted in the geological survey for enhanced attention.<|>\"site-specific design, hazard mitigation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"重冰地段\"<|>\"气象条件\"<|>\"The 'heavy ice zone' is a special condition requiring specific meteorological modeling.<|>\"ice loading, design safety\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"林区\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'forest area' influences vegetation clearance and fire risk assessments.<|>\"environmental impact, clearance requirement\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"主要河流\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'major rivers' require special crossing designs and permits.<|>\"crossing design, environmental compliance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"城镇规划\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'urban planning' determines route alignment and land use compatibility.<|>\"urban integration, zoning\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"海拔高度\"<|>\"气象条件\"<|>\"The 'elevation' affects wind speed, temperature, and icing conditions.<|>\"topographic influence, environmental modeling\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"地形\"<|>\"地质\"<|>\"The 'terrain' influences the 'geological' conditions and foundation design.<|>\"site characterization, earthwork planning\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"地质\"<|>\"基础型式\"<|>\"The 'geology' determines the appropriate 'foundation type' for stability.<|>\"foundation design, site adaptation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"水文\"<|>\"基础型式\"<|>\"The 'hydrology' impacts foundation stability and drainage design.<|>\"drainage, foundation integrity\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"交通运输条件\"<|>\"基础型式\"<|>\"The 'transportation' conditions affect the choice of foundation and material delivery.<|>\"logistics, site access\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电信线路\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'telecom lines' may be affected by electromagnetic interference from the power line.<|>\"EMI, interference mitigation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"无线电台(站)\"<|>\"线路路径\"<|>\"The 'radio stations' are vulnerable to electromagnetic interference and require assessment.<|>\"EMI, signal protection\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"资料来源\"<|>\"气象条件\"<|>\"The 'data sources' are cited in the derivation of meteorological parameters.<|>\"data provenance, technical validation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"换算过程\"<|>\"气象条件\"<|>\"The 'conversion process' is used to adjust raw data into design values.<|>\"data processing, technical calculation\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"分析比较\"<|>\"技术经济比较与论证结果\"<|>\"The 'analysis' leads to the final 'comparison results'<|>\"evaluation method, decision support\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"技术经济比较与论证结果\"<|>\"路径推荐方案\"<|>\"The 'results' inform the selection of the final 'recommended route'.<|>\"decision-making, optimization\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"设计气象条件组合表\"<|>\"气象条件\"<|>\"The 'combination table' summarizes the meteorological conditions used in design.<|>\"design input, data compilation\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"导、地线电气特性表\"<|>\"导线和地线选择\"<|>\"The 'electrical characteristic table' is generated based on conductor and ground wire selection.<|>\"specification documentation, design output\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"光缆物理特性表\"<|>\"导线和地线选择\"<|>\"The 'physical characteristic table' is created for optical cables as part of the same selection process.<|>\"specification documentation, integration\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"绝缘子主要尺寸及机电特性表\"<|>\"绝缘配合\"<|>\"The 'characteristics table' is a direct output of the 'insulation coordination' process.<|>\"technical specification, design deliverable\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"地线绝缘子机械电气特性表\"<|>\"绝缘配合\"<|>\"This table is specific to insulated ground wires and derived from the 'insulation coordination' phase.<|>\"component specification, safety design\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"单基杆塔的耗材量\"<|>\"杆塔型式\"<|>\"The 'material consumption' per tower is determined by the selected 'tower type'.<|>\"material estimation, cost planning\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"主材类型和型号\"<|>\"杆塔型式\"<|>\"The 'material types and models' are specified for each 'tower type'.<|>\"material specification, construction detail\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"标准高度\"<|>\"杆塔型式\"<|>\"The 'standard height' is a key attribute of the 'tower type'.<|>\"dimensional specification, design consistency\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"工程特点\"<|>\"杆塔、基础型式及地质概况\"<|>\"The 'project features' influence the selection of towers and foundations.<|>\"context-driven design, customization\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"利用的原有杆塔\"<|>\"杆塔型式\"<|>\"Existing towers are evaluated for reuse based on design compliance.<|>\"reuse assessment, structural verification\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"验算\"<|>\"利用的原有杆塔\"<|>\"The 'verification' ensures that old towers meet current standards.<|>\"structural assessment, safety check\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"适用性结论\"<|>\"验算\"<|>\"The 'conclusion' states whether the original tower is fit for continued use.<|>\"evaluation outcome, design approval\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"使用性要求\"<|>\"验算\"<|>\"The 'requirements' define the conditions under which an old tower can be used.<|>\"usage criteria, safety threshold\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"技术经济特点\"<|>\"新型杆塔\"<|>\"The 'economic and technical traits' are analyzed to justify the use of new towers.<|>\"feasibility study, innovation assessment\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"使用意义\"<|>\"新型杆塔\"<|>\"The 'practical significance' justifies the adoption of new tower designs.<|>\"strategic value, project benefit\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"安全性和施工可行性\"<|>\"新型基础\"<|>\"These factors are evaluated for new foundation types before implementation.<|>\"risk assessment, constructability analysis\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"开挖方式\"<|>\"特殊地段\"<|>\"The 'excavation method' is adapted for challenging terrain.<|>\"construction adaptation, site-specific method\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"特殊措施\"<|>\"特殊地段\"<|>\"Additional measures are taken in 'special areas' to mitigate risks.<|>\"risk mitigation, contingency planning\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"控制标准\"<|>\"交叉跨越\"<|>\"The 'control standards' set limits for safe crossing distances.<|>\"regulatory compliance, safety margin\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"处理原则\"<|>\"交叉跨越\"<|>\"The 'handling principles' guide how to resolve crossing issues.<|>\"resolution framework, operational guideline\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"影响范围\"<|>\"交叉跨越\"<|>\"The 'impact range' quantifies the extent of disruption from crossings.<|>\"impact assessment, consequence analysis\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"相关数量\"<|>\"交叉跨越\"<|>\"The 'estimated count' of crossings is based on the 'impact range'.<|>\"quantification, project estimation\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"初步停电计划\"<|>\"停电方案设计\"<|>\"The 'draft outage plan' is a core component of the 'outage design'.<|>\"planning stage, outage execution\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"建议\"<|>\"存在问题及建议\"<|>\"The 'recommendations' are provided in response to identified 'problems'.<|>\"problem-solving, proactive guidance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"系统作用和地位\"<|>\"电力系统\"<|>\"The 'role and status' of the system are explained within the 'power system' section.<|>\"system context, functional importance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"配套系统\"<|>\"电力系统\"<|>\"The 'support systems