e cross-sectional area of grounding conductors, determined by fault current and duration.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电缆附件\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '电缆附件' are components used to connect, terminate, or join cables, selected based on voltage level and environment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"排列方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '排列方式' refers to how cables are arranged on supports or in ducts, influenced by space, heat dissipation, and channel capacity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电缆接头\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '电缆接头' is a junction point where two cable segments are joined, placed according to channel layout and segmentation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"资料来源\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '资料来源' refers to the origin of data used in design, such as reports, surveys, or standards, critical for validation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"换算过程\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '换算过程' is the method used to convert measured or estimated data into design values, e.g., from field measurements to design inputs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分析比较\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '分析比较' is a systematic evaluation of alternative designs or materials based on technical and economic criteria.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"投资差额\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '投资差额' is the difference in total project cost between alternative design options, used in decision-making.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"技术条件\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '技术条件' refer to the technical requirements and constraints governing the design, such as load capacity, environmental exposure, and material properties.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主要材料耗量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '主要材料耗量' is the quantity of major materials (steel, concrete, cable) required for each design alternative, used in cost estimation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"现状实景照片\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '现状实景照片' are actual images of the site taken before construction, used to illustrate current conditions in design documentation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地下管线断面图\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The '地下管线断面图' is a cross-sectional drawing showing the layout of underground utilities at a g